Z||000000||fropuff||04-08-2000||04:44 PM||||I found a 1985 Fiero GT for sale in Ontario; it's the nicest one's I've seen so far.  The color is black, and I was wondering if black is a problem.  I see some cars driving down the highway, and they have fingerprints and grease all over them.  I hope not all look this crappy.  Can you help?  Thanks.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Phil||04-08-2000||04:53 PM||||Black has got to be one of the most if the the most difficult color to keep clean, but it sure does look good when it is clean.||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||04-08-2000||06:59 PM||||My theory is that all the straight panels went on the black cars,and all the wavy ones to the lighter colored cars.<BR>As for the cleanliness,it's a matter of how often you wash the car,how you wash the car.<BR>I like dark colors,but won't be painting my car black next time around,that's for sure.||||reg||1
